1
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:04,910
好了 请你们吃完饭了
Okay, I've fed you.

2
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:07,280
有谁想看篮球赛啊
Now, who's ready to watch some basketball?

3
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:08,780
我为什么在看你
Why am I looking at you?

4
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:09,580
不知道
I don't know.

5
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:10,800
不像你 我看穿着短裤
Unlike you, I don't need a reason

6
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:12,240
到处跑的哥们儿不需要理由
to watch a bunch of guys run around in shorts.

7
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:13,760
你已经毁了我的奥运会跳水比赛
Don't ruin this for me like you did

8
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:14,600
别又毁了篮球
with Olympic diving.

9
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,280
-小卡呢 -录下来吧
- Cam? - Recording it.

10
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:18,580
米奇和我要带艾丽克斯和曼尼去看美术展
Mitch and I are taking Alex and Manny to an art exhibit.

11
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:20,360
但当然了 大家都可以一起去
But, of course, everybody is welcome to join.

12
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:23,900
那是战后抽象表现主义的回顾展
It's a retrospective on post-war abstract expressionism.

13
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,860
等等 学校要求的吗
Wait. For school?

14
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,020
不是 是生活所需
No, for life.

15
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:27,100
谢天谢地
Oh, thank God.

16
00:00:27,107 --> 00:00:28,260
我都不知道我们在那场"战后"
I don't even know who we fought

17
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:28,840
是跟谁打的
in the post war.

18
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:30,860
早就告诉你开一辆车就够了
Told you one car was enough.

19
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:32,600
看来只有我们两个啦
Looks like it's just the two amigos.

20
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:33,420
海莉呢
Haley?

21
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,240
真抱歉我吃饱了就要走 外公
Oh, sorry to brunch and bail, grandpa,

22
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,300
但我有个约会
but I've got a date.

23
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:37,560
跟谁啊
Uh, with whom?

24
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:39,180
我在学校认识的帅哥
A gorgeous guy I met at school.

25
00:00:39,380 --> 00:00:41,020
是同学还是扫教室的
Ooh, goes there or cleans there?

26
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:41,500
老妈
Mom.

27
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:42,580
回答她的问题
Answer the question.

28
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:43,580
大家都要走了吗
So everyone's leaving?

29
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:44,680
不 我 我不走啊
No, I'm -- I'm not.

30
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:47,080
早知道就不请你们吃上好的培根了
I wish I had known this before I served the good bacon.

31
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:48,740
你又没请大家吃上好的培根
You did not serve the good bacon.

32
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:50,420
你不是要去买一条小裙子吗
Don't you have a tiny dress to buy?

33
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:53,740
是啊 没错
Yes, we do!

34
00:00:53,740 --> 00:00:55,033
我们请歌洛莉亚带莉莉
We asked Gloria to take Lily

35
00:00:55,033 --> 00:00:56,809
去买一条花童礼裙
to pick out her flower-girl dress.

36
00:00:56,809 --> 00:00:59,540
没错 我们显然无法遵循所有婚礼传统
Yeah, we're clearly not following every wedding tradition,

37
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:01,660
但绝对会有一条裙子是我们
but there will damn sure be one dress

38
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:03,180
两个新郎到婚礼当天才能见到的
the grooms don't see until the big day.

39
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:04,820
我们也请克莱尔一起去
And we also asked Claire to go

40
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:07,040
因为我们认为她的理性
because we thought her sensible style

41
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:09,000
能与歌洛莉亚的豪放互补
nicely complements Gloria's flair.

42
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,572
这样莉莉就不会看起来太过...
That way Lily doesn't end up looking too...

43
00:01:13,122 --> 00:01:14,560
或者太过...
or too...

44
00:01:31,391 --> 00:01:32,879
我的乖儿子
There's my boy.

45
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:33,820
我知道你在跟乔说话
I know you're talking to Joe,

46
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:35,920
不过听到这话还是很开心
but that still feels really good to hear.

47
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:38,120
好了 下班了哦
Okay, clocking out.

48
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:41,040
安迪 如果你愿意的话
You know, Andy, if you want,

49
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:42,560
你可以留下来看比赛
you can stay and watch the game.

50
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:44,240
否则 我就得一个人看了
Otherwise, I'll just be here by myself.

51
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:45,920
我在这儿呢
I'm right here.

52
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:47,329
我也很想看 普先生
I-I'd love to, Mr. P,

53
00:01:47,329 --> 00:01:50,960
但我得去想想送我女友什么周年礼物
but I got to come up with an anniversary gift for my girlfriend.

54
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:52,280
我每年都为她准备不同的礼物
I make her something different every year,

55
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:54,300
比如剪贴本 或漂亮的围巾
like a scrapbook or a nice scarf.

56
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:55,300
今年
This year,

57
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,680
我想也许我可以为她烤些香蕉面包
I was thinking maybe I could bake her some banana bread.

58
00:01:57,680 --> 00:02:00,420
我可是香蕉面包之王
Ohh, I am the king of banana bread.

59
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:01,160
你知道我的秘诀吗
You know my secret?

60
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:02,400
别放坚果
No nuts.

61
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:03,900
这不是什么秘密
Not such a secret.

62
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,980
我以前也总给克莱尔做东西
I used to make stuff for Claire all the time.

63
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:08,400
我相信是我的手艺牢牢锁住了她的心
Pretty sure my artistry is what locked her down.

64
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:09,869
今年我要搞点特别的
I got to make this year's special.

65
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:10,760
她在海岸警卫队
With her in the coast guard,

66
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,420
我都没什么机会去看她
I, like, hardly ever get to see her.

67
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,920
我刚刚想到
Well, this is just off the dome,

68
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:17,460
送她一段好玩的视频怎么样
but, uh, maybe send her a fun video?

69
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:19,960
她确实很喜欢《摇滚年代》
Ooh, she does love "Rock of Ages."

70
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:22,140
或者你也可以录一段自己的视频
Or you could make your own video --

71
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,780
搞点专属浪漫
something romantic and personal

72
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:27,020
我家里有些相当不错的设备
I got some pretty choice equipment back at the house.

73
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:28,140
我很乐意帮你
I'd be happy to help.

74
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,320
-真的吗 -当然了
- Would you really? - Yeah!

75
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:30,440
太好了
Yes!

76
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:32,140
太棒了 马上开工
Great! Let's do it!

77
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:33,540
卢克 伙计 我晚点来接你
Luke, buddy, I'll pick you up later.

78
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:34,600
然后一起去看轮子
We can go check out some wheels.

79
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:36,700
我以为你要留下来看比赛呢
I thought you were gonna stay and watch the game.

80
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,040
我就知道你爱我
I knew you loved me.

81
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:40,400
出去
Get out!

82
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:41,800
走吧
Come on.

83
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:44,520
看轮子 怎么 你已经开始看车了吗
Wheels? What, are you looking at cars already?

84
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:45,560
是陶轮
Pottery wheels.

85
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:47,140
我得选个春季选修课
I have to pick a spring elective,

86
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:48,840
老爸认为我该选陶艺
and dad thinks I should take ceramics

87
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:50,100
因为会有很多女孩选
'cause lots of girls do.

88
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:51,380
你知道大多数姑娘不喜欢什么吗
You know what a lot of girls don't do?

89
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:52,960
修陶艺课的男生
Guys who take ceramics.

90
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:55,000
你们学校有木工场吗
You got a wood shop at your school?

91
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:56,340
我不会制造东西啊
I can't really build stuff.

92
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:58,140
我只会破坏 然后道歉
I mostly take apart and apologize.

93
00:02:58,140 --> 00:02:59,860
你得学会制造东西才行
You got to know how to build things.

94
00:02:59,860 --> 00:03:01,020
我会制造悬念
I can build suspense.

95
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:01,480
怎么制造
How?

96
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:03,120
你看
Well, get this.

97
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:08,160
去车库 马上
Garage. Now.

98
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,780
婚纱店是什么
What's a bridal store?

99
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:15,640
那里有你见过最漂亮的裙子
It's a place with the most wonderful dresses that you have ever seen.

100
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:17,400
我们要给你挑一条最完美的
We're gonna get you the perfect one

101
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:19,420
哪怕花上一天时间
even if it takes us all day.

102
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:21,200
找到了
Found it.

103
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:23,620
不 亲爱的 那是戏服
Oh, no, sweetie. That's a costume.

104
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:25,560
你不能穿着戏服参加婚礼
You can't wear a costume to a wedding.

105
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:27,420
为什么不行 贝拉是个公主
Why not? Belle's a princess.

106
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,040
她面对的是野兽
She faced the beast.

107
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,760
她勇敢反抗市民
She stood up to the townspeople.

108
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:31,940
那你做了什么呢
What have you done?

109
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:35,060
我 成功把车停进了那个
I...got us into that tiny,

110
00:03:35,060 --> 00:03:35,940
小小的停车位上
little parking spot.

111
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:39,520
漂亮的裙子不止公主裙一种
Princess dresses are not the only pretty dresses.

112
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:41,032
我想当公主
I want to be a princess.

113
00:03:41,032 --> 00:03:42,420
我想当公主
I want to be a princess!

114
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:43,580
别再说了
Stop that right now.

115
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:46,136
你的爸爸们想让你买一条花童礼裙
Your dads want you to have a flower-girl dress,

116
00:03:46,136 --> 00:03:47,424
所以我们就要给你买一条花童礼裙
and that's what we're going to get you.

117
00:03:47,424 --> 00:03:48,803
走吧
So march.

118
00:03:50,222 --> 00:03:51,540
停车位上面标着"小车型专用"
It was...it was marked "Compact" and --

119
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:53,240
而我们开的是面包车 所以
and we're driving a minivan, so...

120
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,340
感谢你们请我们来
Hey, thanks for inviting us to this.

121
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:57,320
别客气
Oh, no problem.

122
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:59,080
我很吃惊 我们四人组居然没有
You know, I'm surprised that this particular foursome

123
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:00,840
经常一起出来 考虑到
doesn't hang out more often, considering --

124
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:02,180
这家里只有我们受过教育吗
We're the cultured ones in the family?

125
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:03,560
我不会这么说的
I wouldn't say that.

126
00:04:03,569 --> 00:04:04,928
如果不是跟你们一起的话
Outside of this group.

127
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,000
你知道你爸爸
Did you know your father

128
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,080
去杂货店买书的事情吗
actually goes to the grocery store to buy books?

129
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,420
我知道 是啊
I did know that, yeah.

130
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:11,560
我还知道让我姐姐睡觉的
I also know that the best way

131
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:13,120
最好办法就是
to get my sister to fall asleep is to --

132
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:14,440
给她看有字幕的电影
Show her a movie with subtitles.

133
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:15,480
晚安 妈妈[法语]
Bonne nuit, mama.

134
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:17,060
我们应该庆幸且感激
We should be nice and grateful

135
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:18,540
我们今天能够在这个私人画廊
that we have this day to spend together

136
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:19,960
一起度过美好时光
in our own private salon.

137
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:21,320
别跟我妈说那话
Don't tell my mom that.

138
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:22,780
她会跳出来说要染头发
She'll show up and ask to get her roots done.

139
00:04:23,253 --> 00:04:25,468
-曼尼 -那是真的 是真的
- Manny! - That's true. It's true.

140
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:28,740
谢谢 曼尼
Thanks, manny.

141
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:31,000
我好期待这场展览
I am so excited for this exhibit.

142
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:32,760
我超级崇拜康丁斯基
I'm such an admirer of Kandinsky.

143
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:34,200
他可是被誉为
You know, he was credited

144
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:37,040
创作真正意义上抽象作品的第一人啊
with painting the first truly abstract work.

145
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:37,620
是吗
Is that so?

146
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:39,880
说实话 跟这三个家伙
To be honest, I was a little nervous

147
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:41,200
一起出来 我有点紧张
about holding my own with those three,

148
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:44,260
所以我做了些关于康丁斯基的功课
so I did a little boning up on Kandinsky.

149
00:04:44,260 --> 00:04:46,800
反正多记几个知识点是不会错的
Figured it couldn't hurt to have a few facts in my pocket.

150
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:49,860
我的后备计划是上手摸展品然后被赶出去
My backup plan was to touch a painting and get thrown out.

151
00:04:50,453 --> 00:04:51,720
女士 你好 打扰一下
Miss, hi. Excuse me.

152
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:54,000
可以告诉我们康丁斯基的画展在哪里吗
Can you tell us where the Kandinsky exhibit is?

153
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,220
卫斯理·康丁斯基
You know, Wassily Kandinsky?

154
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:56,760
生于莫斯科 一个茶商的儿子
Born in Moscow, son of a tea merchant?

155
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:58,860
抱歉 那场画展是临时的
I'm sorry. That exhibit was temporary.

156
00:04:59,180 --> 00:04:59,880
已经结束了
It's closed.

157
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:00,400
什么
What?

158
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:01,380
不是吧
No.

159
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:03,500
我喜欢这幅马蒂斯的画
Oh, I love this Matisse.

160
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:05,340
这是他最后的作品之一
You know this is one of his final works.

161
00:05:05,420 --> 00:05:07,580
他健康状况恶化使他开始探索剪纸
His failing health led to his exploration of paper cutouts.

162
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:10,200
是啊 我记得他称之为"用剪刀作画"
Ah, yes. I believe he called it "Painting with scissors."

163
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,280
而且他跟毕加索生活在同一时代
And he was also a contemporary of Picasso.

164
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:14,320
你完全能看出他们是如何影响彼此的
You can definitely see how they influenced each other.

165
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:15,293
是吧 小卡
Right, Cam?

166
00:05:15,341 --> 00:05:17,430
这画一下让我想起了...
Uh, well, you know, it really reminds me...

167
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:19,231
康丁斯基
Of, uh, Kandinsky.

168
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:20,560
为什么
How so?

169
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,680
看起来不大一样 但材质很相似
Well, not so much in look, more in texture.

170
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:23,289
不 小卡
No, no, Cam!

171
00:05:23,289 --> 00:05:24,612
先生 请不要碰画作
No, please, sir, don't touch the art.

172
00:05:24,612 --> 00:05:25,703
抱歉 我马上离开这里
I'm sorry. I'll leave the premises.

173
00:05:25,703 --> 00:05:26,900
不 没关系
No, it's -- it's fine.

174
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:28,560
您后退几步就行了
Just take a few steps back.

175
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:34,420
贝丝 我愿意游过满是鲨鱼的深海
Beth, I would swim the deepest, sharkiest oceans

176
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:35,460
来和你在一起
to be with you.

177
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:36,800
你们在干什么
What are you doing?

178
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:37,460
停拍
Cut!

179
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:39,420
这样就穿帮了
Well, now we have a blooper reel.

180
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:42,120
我们在为安迪的女友拍视频情书
We're making a video love letter for Andy's girlfriend.

181
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:44,980
你爸爸用他的电脑来设置很棒的背景
Your dad uses his computer to put in cool backgrounds

182
00:05:44,980 --> 00:05:47,000
而我表演为了和她在一起
while I act out all the things that

183
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:47,840
我愿意做的事
I would do to be with her,

184
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:50,410
比如游过深海 或者爬山
